cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Novum Pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alberto
    family-names: Sola
    email: albertosola2002@gmail.com
    affiliation: Università degli Studi di Torino (UniTo)
repository-code: "https://github.com/alberto-sola/novum_pipeline"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Snakemake workflow for predicting miRNA targets in
  bacterial coding sequences with RNAhybrid. Optionally
  calibrates RNAhybrid's extreme-value statistics per
  miRNA via RNAcalibrate, so each query is scored against
  its own null distribution rather than a single species
  default. RNAhybrid is parallelised across (miRNA × target
  chunk) pairs with GNU Parallel; the raw output is tidied,
  annotated with FASTA-derived gene/locus/protein metadata,
  rendered as human-readable alignment summaries, and
  optionally plotted with ggplot2. A bundled PyWebView GUI
  provides a no-CLI interface for editing the config and
  launching runs.
keywords:
  - snakemake
  - pipeline
  - RNAhybrid
  - miRNAs
  - genomes
  - bacteria
  - python
  - tidyverse

